# Task: print disk usage for a mount point or directory in POSIX df format.
# Program: this file.
# Run: execute docs/recipes/server-disk-usage.program
#      execute docs/recipes/server-disk-usage.program --input path=/var
# Test with fakes: put a fake `df` earlier on PATH that prints its arguments. Expect
#   -P and the path, with the default path of /.
# Explain: the output is df's own table; the program adds nothing.
# Replaces (Bash): df -P "${1:-/}"
accept path as text with default "/"
run "df" with arguments ["-P", path]
